{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GGBCdP8ru1qWUFLJDCooKC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Domain research: OpenAPI 3.1 vs 3.0.3","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:domain-researcher","prompt":"You are resolving a clarify question for a SpecKit autopilot workflow. Research industry best practices and official documentation to recommend an evidence-based answer.\n\n**Question (Q1):**\nShould we adopt OpenAPI 3.1 (industry-current) or OpenAPI 3.0.3 (matching what the constitution standardized on for our existing services)?\n\n**Your task:**\nResearch this from a domain/industry-best-practices perspective only. Do NOT consider project-specific constitution constraints — that is the spec-context-analyst's job. Focus on:\n\n1. **Current state of OpenAPI 3.1 adoption (as of 2026)**: Which major tools, generators, validators, and frameworks support 3.1 vs. 3.0.3? Is 3.1 considered the de facto standard now, or are there still gaps?\n2. **Technical differences that matter**: JSON Schema 2020-12 alignment in 3.1, nullable handling, webhooks, type unions — which differences are practical (affect everyday API design) vs. theoretical?\n3. **Migration cost / interop**: If a team is on 3.0.3 today, what is the realistic effort to move to 3.1? Are there breaking changes for consumers, or is it mostly additive?\n4. **Industry direction**: What do OpenAPI Initiative, Spectral, Stoplight, Redocly, and major cloud providers (AWS, Azure, Google) recommend in 2026?\n\nUse Tavily search and Context7 docs (resolve \"openapi\" library ID first) to ground your answer. Cite specific sources.\n\n**Return format (be concise):**\n- **Recommendation:** [3.1 | 3.0.3 | depends-on-X]\n- **Confidence:** [high | medium | low]\n- **Key evidence:** 3-5 bullet points with source citations\n- **Caveats:** Any conditions where the recommendation flips\n\nDo not write files. Do not synthesize across other analysts. Return your answer as your final message."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
